    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="1203" n="1193" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/12–2145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Robertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-21T18:00:00-05:00">December 21,
                            1945—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2039. In accordance with President’s Directive,<anchor n="93" xml:id="d912-f1"/>
                    Treas[ury] has stopped all financial negotiations with the Chinese Government.
                    (For Adler from the Secretary of the Treas.)</p>
                <p>You are instructed, therefore, to cease, until further notice, negotiations with
                    the Chinese Govt on Treasury’s proposal to apply the yuan proceeds of surplus
                    property against the Army’s yuan obligations to China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d912-f1" n="93" xml:id="d912-f1-content">
                <p>Quoted in telegram No. 2022, December 19, 7 p.m., to the Chargé in China, <ref
                        target="#pg1376">p. 1376</ref>.</p>
            </note>
